    description: "Residual of the WI-gopok-zanij-zafib-ralaj-fukaz-gavol-purib-poliv sweep (branch jgstern-agent/fix/gopok). That branch scoped four name lookups by the languages their mechanism reaches (orm, subprocess_cli, argparse_dispatch, go_cobra) and gave the shared helper LinkerContext.find_symbols_by_name a languages= parameter. The sweep of packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/ (every name-keyed symbol index and every find_symbols_by_name caller) found these further lookups that admit a same-named symbol in ANY language. Each is a separate code path, so none was changed; each needs its own verification (premise read in code only, NOT reproduced live, NOT measured on the corpus):\n\n1. di_resolution.py _create_di_registers_edges, nestjs:module bindings (~line 697): syms_by_name indexes every class/interface by name, any language; a NestJS @Module provider name (a TypeScript source) can resolve to a same-named Python/Java class. Reachable set: javascript/typescript.\n2. type_hierarchy.py _resolve_method_class_id (~line 380): a method is assigned to a class by the class-name part of its name; same-file wins, else 'first candidate' in symbol order, any language. A Go method declared in a different file from its struct (normal in Go) can be attached to a same-named Python/Java class. Reachable set: the method's own language.\n3. grpc.py _resolve_unresolved_grpc_edges (~line 1143): an unresolved GO call to RegisterFooServer picks the first symbol named RegisterFooServer from ctx.symbols in any language. Reachable set: go (plus whatever language the linker's own minted symbols carry -- check before filtering).\n4. decorator_dispatch.py: dispatch sites are matched by function NAME (run_all_analyzers ...) and handlers by decorator NAME, both in any language; a same-named JS function becomes a dispatch site for Python handlers. Low likelihood (hypergumbo-specific registries).\n5. route_handler.py link_routes_to_handlers symbol_by_name (~line 657): single-valued, language-agnostic name index used to resolve route handler refs; a Python framework route can resolve to a same-named symbol in another language. Overlaps WI-hahud-hidoz-namit-kodov-duruh-zafoj-loput-zosol (same-named view collision), which is about collisions in general, not the language axis.\n6. annotation_convention.py @hg:dispatches X (~line 343): any-language name index. Needs a RULING first, not a fix: the directive is user-declared and might deliberately name a cross-language target.\n\nChecked and NOT in this family (filtered already, or cross-language by design): inheritance (filters c.language == child.language), inherited_calls (_same_language_class_ids, INV-milud), containment (same-language preference), jni / cgo / lua_ffi / napi / pyffi / ruby_ffi / solidity_abi (destination set filtered by language), react_component, jackson_dispatch, kafka_streams_dispatch, view_template_laravel / _spring (language-filtered), tauri_ipc / wasm_bindgen (keyed on Rust-only annotations), otp (erlang), database_query (SQL tables are reached from any language by design), dependency (manifest symbols), graphql / graphql_resolver / grpc proto services / http / websocket / message_queue (cross-language by design).\n\nFix shape: LinkerContext.find_symbols_by_name(name, languages=...) where the code path uses it; an explicit language test at index build otherwise. Each fix needs a two-sided fixture (lone foreign namesake -> no edge; foreign namesake beside the right one -> no INV-zuhub demotion), as WI-gopok's tests do."  # 7182
    fields: {}  # 7182
- op: discuss  # 57c8
  at: '2026-10-25T11:06:06Z'  # 57c8
  by: agent  # 57c8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 57c8
  clock: 2  # 57c8
  nonce: 57c8  # 57c8
  message: "Two more members of this family found by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (verifier read the code), neither in the list above: - airflow_framework_dispatch.py: (low impact) `_find_airflow_subclasses` passes `language=None` (L134), and `_build_method_index` (L148-158) has no language filter, so classes in any language match, even though the docstring says \"Python-internal\" (L41-42), the CNF comment says \"airflow is Python-only\" (L165), and the `_build_method_index` docstring says \"Index Python methods\". The django and third-party siblings pass `language=\"python\"` (django_orm_dispatch.py:249, _third_party_bases.py:196). This is not a regression: `git show b5146af1d8` shows that the pre-refactor inline loop had no language filter either, and `language=None` preserved that. -- evidence (repro, scratchpad/verify/tmp/v07_airflow.py): a Java `class MyOp` with `base_classes=[\"BaseOperator\"]` plus a Java method `MyOp.execute` -> `_find_airflow_subclasses` returns `[('MyOp', 'java', {'post_execute': (), 'execute_complete': (), 'execute': (), 'on_kill': (), 'pre_execute': ()})]`. - pyffi.py: Phase 2 bridges unresolved calls from any language, not only Python -- evidence: L459-466 iterate `for edge in edges:` with only the `test_symbol_ids` and `:unresolved` checks. The comment `# Format: \"python:path:0-0:name:unresolved\"` is never enforced, and the wrapper passes the full `ctx.edges` (L582). Repro (scratchpad/verify/tmp/v08md/pf.py): a PyO3 `encode` (annotations `[{\"name\":\"pyfunction\"}]`) plus a JS edge `javascript:web/app.js:1-3:main:function -> javascript:web/app.js:0-0:encode:unresolved` produces `javascript:web/app.js:1-3:main:function -> rust:src/lib.rs:1-5:encode:function {'bridge_kind': 'ffi', 'framework_dispatch': 'pyo3_bridge', ...}`. Rust's own unresolved `encode` calls would bridge the same way. Fix: require `edge.src` to be a Python symbol, e.g. `edge.src in python_ids`."  # 57c8
